; The two live tiers in the debug spawner. t3 is retired and is
; deliberately absent - a withdrawn item in the spawner is a withdrawn
; item somebody will spawn.

![amplayer_magazine_pouch_t1]
$spawn = "equipment\layered\magazine pouch small"

![amplayer_magazine_pouch_t2]
$spawn = "equipment\layered\magazine pouch medium"

; ============================================================
;  AND THE RETIRED ONE, PUT WHERE IT CANNOT BE PICKED BY ACCIDENT
;
;  Saying a section is retired does not remove it from the spawner -
;  it inherits $spawn from its parent and turns up under whatever
;  branch that names, which is how these were still appearing after
;  being withdrawn from trade and craft.
;
;  Removing the key is not possible from an override file, so the next
;  best thing is to send them somewhere clearly marked. They are
;  grouped under one leaf that says what they are.
; ============================================================

![amplayer_magazine_pouch_t3]
$spawn = "equipment\layered\zz retired\magazine pouch t3"
